WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
That suspected

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.135
Chinese surveillance balloon

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.203
spotted in the skies over

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.771
the continental U.S.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.772
has sparked concerns

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.940
about national security

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.309
and diplomacy regarding Beijing.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.011
Is it more about symbolism

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.412
than substance?

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.179
Secretary of State

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.047
Anthony Blinken

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.715
was due to travel to China this week,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.017
and he postponed his trip,

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.119
calling the balloons infiltration of U.S.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.320
airspace a, quote,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.621
irresponsible act

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.722
that created conditions

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.258
that undermine the purpose of the trip.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.893
The public first learned of the balloons

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.061
existence Thursday

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.929
while it was over Montana

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.231
which is home to US

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.732
intercontinental ballistic missile

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.101
silos and strategic bomber bases.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.837
China is saying that it's all innocent.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.571
On Friday,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.339
a spokesperson

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.240
for the Chinese foreign

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.109
ministry said this is a civilian airship

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.544
used for research,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.980
mainly meteorological purposes

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.381
affected by the westerlies

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.382
and with limited self

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.517
steering capability.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.185
The airship deviated far

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.586
from its planned course.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.854
The Chinese side regrets

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.056
the unintended entry

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.090
of the airship

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.559
into airspace due to force major.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:00.393
But the U.S.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.027
State Department

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:01.928
called it a, quote, clear

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.197
violation of our sovereignty

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.199
as well as international law.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.500
The Pentagon said on Friday

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.202
the balloon currently does not pose

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.271
a military or political threat.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.573
And a senior US defense official told CNN

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.141
that military officials had advised

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.109
President Biden

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.111
not to shoot the balloon down

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.946
due to fear over the debris

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.781
posing a safety threat.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.450
I tweeted out a quick take last night.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.452
I said The violation of our sovereign

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:28.021
airspace should not be a partizan issue.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.156
Many are questioning why

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.157
we aren't taking it out

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.625
and they especially are coming

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.560
from the right.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.994
Florida Senator Marco Rubio,

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.929
a member of Congress,

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.297
so-called Gang of Eight,

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:37.997
who are briefed

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.933
on national intelligence matters.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.633
He tweeted this

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.902
It was a mistake to not shoot down

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.503
that Chinese

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.370
spy balloon

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.071
when it was over

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.407
a sparsely populated area.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.142
This is not some hot air balloon.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.843
It has a large

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.377
payload of sensors, roughly

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.146
the size of two city busses

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.114
and the ability

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.949
to maneuver independently.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.716
Utah Senator

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.885
Mitt Romney wrote a big Chinese

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.120
balloon in the sky

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.621
and millions of Chinese TikTok

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.922
balloons on our phones.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.024
Let's shut them all down.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:05.892
Over on Truth

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.527
Social former President Trump,

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.962
much more succinct

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.164
shoot down the balloon, he said.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.332
Joining me now to discuss

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.032
is retired

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.434
Air Force Lieutenant General

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.236
David Deptula,

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:16.836
who was the Air

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.037
Force's first chief

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.606
of intelligence, surveillance

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.174
and reconnaissance.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.142
He's a fighter pilot

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.244
with more than 3000 flying hours.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.411
He was the principal attack

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.646
planner for the operation

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.648
Desert Storm Air campaign

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.782
commander of no fly

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.618
operations over Iraq in the late nineties

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.552
and served on two

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.953
congressional commissions

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.021
focused on America's

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.723
future defense strategy

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.290
He's currently

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.459
the dean of the Mitchell Institute

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.394
for Aerospace Studies. General.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.829
Thanks so much for being here.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.098
What exactly are the options

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.499
when an object like this is

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.234
at 60,000 feet

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.504
Well, Michael,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.038
first, thanks

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.440
for having me on and

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.375
really appreciate it.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.610
It's a great question.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.846
There are several options

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.649
Some of them depend upon the location of

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.050
the balloon.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.918
What makes this

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.653
a complicated situation

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.755
is that it's up at 60,000 feet

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.992
And there aren't a lot of

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.661
aircraft that are capable

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.895
that can go up there

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.498
with the kind of means to shoot it down

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:18.965
today.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.901
You're looking at the F-22 or the F-15

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.237
and then the weapons

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.806
that can be used to actually

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:27.840
shoot the balloon down.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.174
Of course,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.343
there's surface to air missile systems,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.878
but those are fixed.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:35.281
And we really don't have any of those

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.083
operationally deployed

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.252
in the continental United States.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.354
So the options are, you know, added to

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.623
fighter aircraft.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.091
Do you know that it's necessarily

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.627
going to fall over a particular area,

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.730
meaning if you use the weapon systems

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.764
that you just identified

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.733
and you're successful in hitting it,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.001
like how long is it

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.236
going to take for it to come down?

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.904
And do you necessarily know where it

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:58.471
will land

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.174
Well, that's a great question.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.676
And the short answer is no.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.577
You don't know

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.946
with any degree of accuracy

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:10.083
because it depends upon just how large

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:13.620
the hole or the damage

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.921
done to the balloon,

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:15.888
which will determine

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.157
how fast it will come down

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.092
and then what you hit

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.660
I mean, you hit the balloon

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.794
and you can penetrate it

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.530
and it can come down at a certain rate

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.099
if it's all in one piece.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.166
Probably no big deal.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.135
It's going to land in one place.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.237
But if you hit the payload package

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.772
and destroy that,

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.140
now you have the debris

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.475
that's going to be scattered.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.210
But the fact of the matter is,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.678
the the dog on thing

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:39.779
should have been shot down

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.446
before it

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.582
penetrated the territory

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.317
of our sovereign airspace.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.152
Your introductory conclusion

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.720
was a pretty good one.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.689
Because what's really a more concern

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.391
than the sensor package

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.760
that this Chinese balloon is carrying is

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.695
why did we let a potential adversary

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.462
air vehicle

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.665
penetrate the sovereign territory

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.333
of Canada, the United States?

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.968
It should have been neutralized

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.303
as it entered our air defense

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.871
identification zone.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:07.573
So of course, we in

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.107
the public

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.842
only learned of this on Thursday.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.210
I think what you're saying, General,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.512
is that the military

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.781
probably had knowledge for much longer,

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:16.683
including preceding

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.251
when it entered our airspace.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.986
Is that what you're saying?

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:21.587
Yeah, absolutely.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.855
We have this organization,

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.023
it's known as the North American

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.059
Aerospace Defense Command.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:27.860
It's a combined organization

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.063
of the United States and Canada.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:30.663
It provides

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.865
aerospace warning, air sovereignty

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.901
and then protection.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.170
At least it's supposed to protect Canada

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.173
in the continental United States.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.909
But I would suggest to you, too,

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.144
and this is a discussion for a whole

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:45.912
nother program,

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.914
but I think like most of the capabilities

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.415
of the United States

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:49.949
Air Force,

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.184
they've been underfunded

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:51.651
and allowed

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.820
to atrophy over the past 30 years.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.755
And this is a consequence

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.058
General, how's it going to end?

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.060
I pointed out a political reality

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:01.761
that the president's

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:02.829
going to speak to the nation

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.997
and to the Congress on Tuesday night.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.165
And the reports

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.300
that we're getting suggests

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.868
that this thing will hit the Atlantic

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.203
probably by the end of the

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.572
the weekend, depending upon the wind.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.041
So you think he's going to take it out?

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:15.908
You think the president's going

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.210
to give the order and the U.S.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.913
military will take it out before Tuesday?

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.982
You know, that's

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.618
that's a I don't want to be facetious.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.220
That's a question for the president.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.454
I really don't know.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.790
I would tell you that my opinion is

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:34.460
he'll probably let it go.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.129
But the fact of the matter is,

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:38.931
this is not an inconsequential act.

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:41.300
And it should have been shot down prior

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.503
to violating a sovereign U.S. airspace.

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.606
So my poll question today asks

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.473
whether this is a matter

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.942
of national security or national pride

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:53.613
What's your answer to that question?

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.581
National security.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.184
I mean, look, this particular

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:58.751
balloon

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.487
may have been just a weather balloon that

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.756
flown off course.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.991
I don't believe that.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:06.793
I don't think it was an accident.

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.995
I believe it was a Chinese testing

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.898
the U.S. reaction.

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:12.432
But, you know,

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.700
another balloon could carry, for example,

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:18.471
an MP device, electromagnetic pulse

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:22.275
that could shut down segments of our U.S.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.743
electric power grid.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:26.746
So it's not an inconsequential fact

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.583
that this balloon has been sent to fly

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.251
over the continental United States.

